# Browser protections for every page and file the app serves.
#
# Static assets are answered by Cloudflare before the Worker runs, so these
# are set here rather than in code. /api/* and /p/* are the Worker's own and
# set their own headers (lib/http.ts).
#
# Content-Security-Policy is deliberately narrow: it governs *scripts* and
# framing, which is where an injected string turns into somebody else's code
# running with a customer's session. Images, fonts and connections are left
# open because customers paste logos, product photos and embeds from anywhere,
# and a policy that breaks their own pictures would be switched off within a
# week. `script-src` has no 'unsafe-inline' and no 'unsafe-eval': the built app
# needs neither, and together they are most of what XSS relies on.
# YouTube's player API is the one third-party script (AI Shorts preview).
#
# microphone=(self) because voice prompts use it; camera and location are not
# used anywhere and are refused.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: script-src 'self' https://www.youtube.com https://s.ytimg.com; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; frame-ancestors 'self'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), geolocation=(), microphone=(self), payment=(), usb=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin-allow-popups

# The chat widget is embedded on customers' own sites, so it must be loadable
# cross-origin; everything above still applies to it.
/widget.js
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
